    "note": "Reported at NUCLEOTIDE resolution rather than as an exon, which is why no literature sweep found it: GenBank AF289510.1 (421 bp, 'Homo sapiens TCF12-TEC fusion protein mRNA, partial cds', submitted 25-JUL-2000, citing PMID 11156374) splits 1..263 on chromosome 15 (15q21) and 264..421 on chromosome 9 (9q22). Mapped against the committed transcript models the donor side ends at TCF12 exon 5 and no other exon, the acceptor side begins at NR4A3 exon 3 and no other exon, and the seam is identical to the one the screens ran on. Corroborated independently by PMID 12826747, a TCF12 gene-structure paper reporting 21 exons — the same count as the committed model — and that 'intron 5 in the TCF12 gene corresponds to the region involved in a translocation, t(9;15)(q22;q21)'. ⚠ ONE TUMOUR: neither breakpoint series behind the coverage ladder contains a TCF12-rearranged tumour, so this seam has a resolved junction and no within-partner distribution.",
